    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d103">

                <pb facs="0110" n="104" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg104"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dun to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 104.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tokyo, Japan</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-02-27"><hi rendition="#italic">February 27, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received March 21.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a
                    clipping from the Japan Mail of the 25th instant, giving a translation of a
                    speech on the subject of the proposed Korean loan delivered by Count Ito,
                    minister president of state, before the lower house of the Imperial Diet on the
                    21st instant.</p>
                <p>The bill, as recommended by the Government, authorizing a loan of 3,000,000 yen
                    to the Korean Government has been passed by the House of Representatives.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin Dun.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d103-a1.xml" xpointer="d103-a1"/>
            </div>
